---

<DocsLayout
  title="Packages and apps"
  subtitle="Npm names, directories, and the workspace dependencies each package.json actually declares."
  description="CADCAMFUN workspace packages and apps: paths, ownership, dependency direction, and the commands that typecheck them."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="packages" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Packages</h2>
    <p>
      Libraries live under <code>packages/</code>. The root <code>package.json</code> workspace
      glob is <code>packages/*</code>, so every directory here is a workspace, including this docs
      site. Effect is <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code> wherever it appears, because
      <code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code> requires that release. Do not bump it in one package.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Package</th><th>Path</th><th>Declares a dependency on</th><th>Owns</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/db</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/db</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code>, <code>drizzle-orm@1.0.0-beta.22</code>. No other workspace package.</td>
          <td>Drizzle schema (<code>src/schema.ts</code>), migrations (<code>drizzle/</code>), <code>Database</code> service (<code>src/index.ts</code>), CLI migrate (<code>src/migrate.ts</code>). SQLite via <code>bun:sqlite</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/core</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/core</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code> only. Hot loops stay plain functions.</td>
          <td>CAD in <code>src/cad</code>, CAM and G-code in <code>src/cam</code>, drawing in <code>src/drawing</code>. No database, network, or filesystem.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/api</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/api</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code>, <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>, <code>zod</code>.</td>
          <td>Schema-first HttpApi groups in <code>src/groups</code>, shared domain schemas, generated clients in <code>src/sdk</code> and <code>src/client</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/ai</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/ai</code></td>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/api</code>, <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>, <code>effect</code>, <code>ai</code> 7.x, <code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code>, <code>@ai-sdk/*</code>.</td>
          <td>nikcli embedded host and AI SDK v7, as Effect services. Source under <code>src/nikcli</code>, <code>src/tools</code>, <code>src/skills</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/plugin-sdk</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/plugin-sdk</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code>, <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>.</td>
          <td>Public plugin types: <code>manifest.ts</code>, <code>plugin.ts</code>, <code>capability.ts</code>, <code>context.ts</code>, <code>test-host.ts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/vcs</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/vcs</code></td>
          <td>None.</td>
          <td>Git-compatible history: <code>object.ts</code>, <code>repository.ts</code>, <code>snapshot.ts</code>, <code>diff.ts</code>, <code>github.ts</code>, <code>store.ts</code>, <code>transport.ts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/workflow</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/workflow</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code> only.</td>
          <td>Actions-style schema (<code>schema.ts</code>), triggers (<code>trigger.ts</code>), runner (<code>run.ts</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/httpapi-codegen</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/httpapi-codegen</code></td>
          <td><code>effect</code>, <code>prettier</code>. Dev: <code>@effect/platform-bun</code>.</td>
          <td>Generates clients. <code>@cadcamfun/api</code>’s <code>generate</code> script writes <code>packages/api/src/sdk</code> and <code>packages/api/src/client</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@nikoemme_/cadcamfun-nikcli-plugin</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/nikcli-plugin</code></td>
          <td><code>zod</code> only.</td>
          <td>Tools a standalone nikcli uses against a running app. The catalogue is the app’s. The plugin does not keep a second copy.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/web</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/web</code></td>
          <td>Astro 5, Tailwind 3. No <code>@cadcamfun/*</code> runtime dependency.</td>
          <td>This documentation site. It does not import the sidecar or the database.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <code>packages/nikcli-plugin</code> is the bridge for a nikcli process outside the desktop
      (a terminal, another machine, CI). It presents the same action catalogue the embedded host
      registers, and it calls the running sidecar to invoke those actions. It is not the embedded
      host. The embedded host is <code>packages/ai</code>, loaded by <code>apps/sidecar</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Public entry points are the <code>exports</code> map in each <code>package.json</code>.
      <code>@cadcamfun/db</code> exports <code>.</code> and <code>./schema</code>.
      <code>@cadcamfun/api</code> exports <code>.</code> and <code>./sdk</code>
      (<code>src/sdk/generated/index.ts</code>). The others export <code>.</code> as
      <code>src/index.ts</code>. Import those paths. Do not deep-import a file that is not exported,
      from another package.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="apps" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Apps</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Package</th><th>Path</th><th>Workspace dependencies</th><th>Owns</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/sidecar</code></td>
          <td><code>apps/sidecar</code></td>
          <td><code>ai</code>, <code>api</code>, <code>core</code>, <code>db</code>, <code>plugin-sdk</code>, <code>vcs</code>, <code>workflow</code></td>
          <td>Bun Effect server. Entry <code>src/main.ts</code>. HTTP handlers in <code>src/http</code>, services in <code>src/services</code>, repositories in <code>src/repos</code>, plugin host in <code>src/plugins</code>, wiring in <code>src/layers.ts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/desktop</code></td>
          <td><code>apps/desktop</code></td>
          <td><code>api</code>, <code>core</code></td>
          <td>SolidJS + Vite UI in <code>src/</code>, Tauri v2 shell in <code>src-tauri/</code>. Three.js is a direct dependency (<code>three</code> ^0.180).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/mobile</code></td>
          <td><code>apps/mobile</code></td>
          <td><code>api</code> only</td>
          <td>Expo iOS companion (package version 6.0.0). Thin client of a paired desktop. Native pairing socket in <code>modules/companion-net</code>. Scripts: <code>expo start --dev-client</code>, <code>expo run:ios</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The README rule is that the desktop imports API types only. The desktop manifest also depends
      on <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>, and the viewport plus the CAD and CAM features import
      geometry and toolpath helpers from it. Mobile does not. Neither app depends on
      <code>@cadcamfun/db</code>. The sidecar is the process that opens
      <code>cadcamfun.db</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Desktop source layout, from <code>apps/desktop/src/README.md</code> and the README at the
      repo root:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>src/app/</code> — shell, route table (<code>routes.tsx</code>), API client. No product logic in the shell.</li>
      <li><code>src/pages/</code> — one-line route adapters. No logic.</li>
      <li><code>src/features/&lt;name&gt;/</code> — one folder per product area. Inside, only the folders that area needs: <code>screens/</code>, <code>components/</code>, <code>hooks/</code>, <code>lib/</code>, <code>store/</code>, <code>types/</code>, <code>api/</code>, <code>styles/</code>.</li>
      <li><code>src/shared/</code> — <code>ui/</code>, <code>components/</code>, <code>state/</code>. Move code here when a second feature needs it.</li>
      <li><code>src/styles/</code> — global CSS. Feature CSS stays in the feature.</li>
      <li><code>src/viewport/</code> — 2D/3D engine (<code>editor2d</code>, <code>view3d</code>, <code>spatial</code>, <code>units.ts</code>).</li>
      <li><code>src/i18n/</code> — translation tables. Default locale <code>en</code>.</li>
      <li><code>src/testing/</code> — fake API and core-flow tests.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Feature directories present under <code>apps/desktop/src/features</code>:
      <code>admin</code>, <code>ai</code>, <code>analytics</code>, <code>auth</code>,
      <code>billing</code>, <code>cad</code>, <code>cam</code>, <code>chat</code>,
      <code>companion</code>, <code>costs</code>, <code>dashboard</code>, <code>legal</code>,
      <code>library</code>, <code>marketplace</code>, <code>mcp</code>, <code>organizations</code>,
      <code>plugins</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>projects</code>, <code>settings</code>,
      <code>toolpaths</code>. Imports between features go through each feature’s public files.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="direction" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Direction</h2>
    <p>
      The README writes the allowed arrows with no cycles:
      <code>core</code> ← <code>api</code> ← sidecar;
      <code>db</code> ← sidecar;
      <code>ai</code> and <code>plugin-sdk</code> ← sidecar.
      The desktop imports API types only. <code>core</code> and <code>api</code> must not import
      <code>db</code>. The manifests add two arrows the one-line summary does not draw:
      <code>core</code> ← <code>ai</code>, <code>core</code> ← <code>plugin-sdk</code>, and
      <code>core</code> ← desktop. <code>vcs</code> and <code>workflow</code> are sidecar
      dependencies. <code>workflow</code> does not depend on <code>vcs</code> in its
      <code>package.json</code>; the sidecar composes them.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="text" title="Who may import whom">
{`packages/core        no @cadcamfun/db, no I/O in hot loops
packages/api         @cadcamfun/core only
packages/ai          @cadcamfun/api, @cadcamfun/core
packages/plugin-sdk  @cadcamfun/core
packages/vcs         no workspace dependencies
packages/workflow    effect only
apps/sidecar         ai, api, core, db, plugin-sdk, vcs, workflow
apps/desktop         api, core
apps/mobile          api
packages/web         none of the above`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      <code>specs/</code> is the contract for scope and APIs. It is not a package. Sequence of
      remaining work is <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code>. The current step is RM-01, the action
      catalogue (<code>specs/roadmap/01-action-catalogue.md</code>). Units inside
      <code>packages/core</code> are millimetres and radians. Degrees and G-code decimal formatting
      stay at the UI and post boundary.
    </p>
    <DocCallout title="Legacy code stays out" type="warn">
      <p>
        <code>.reference/</code> is the old Next.js and Prisma app. It is git-ignored and read-only.
        v6 does not import it. A type you remember from Prisma is re-declared in
        <code>packages/db/src/schema.ts</code> or in <code>packages/api</code>, with the same table
        and column names, not with a path back into <code>.reference/</code>.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="commands" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <p>
      From the repository root. <code>bunx tsc -p</code> is the README check for one project.
      <code>bun run --filter &lt;pkg&gt; typecheck</code> runs that package’s own script, which is
      <code>tsgo</code> for every package except <code>@cadcamfun/mobile</code> and
      <code>@cadcamfun/web</code> (those use <code>tsc</code>).
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="From the repo root">
{`bun test packages/core
bunx tsc -p packages/core/tsconfig.json
bun test apps/sidecar
bunx tsc -p apps/sidecar/tsconfig.json
bun run --filter @cadcamfun/api coverage
bun run generate
bun run generate:check
bun run --filter @cadcamfun/web dev`}
    </DocCode>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Root script</th><th>Resolves to</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run db:generate</code></td>
          <td><code>drizzle-kit generate</code> in <code>packages/db</code> (<code>drizzle.config.ts</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run db:migrate</code></td>
          <td><code>bun src/migrate.ts</code> in <code>packages/db</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run generate</code></td>
          <td><code>packages/api/scripts/generate-clients.ts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run generate:check</code></td>
          <td>The same script with <code>--check</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun test packages apps</code></td>
          <td>README suite. Does not include <code>scripts/</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run test</code></td>
          <td><code>bun test packages apps scripts</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run typecheck</code></td>
          <td><code>turbo run typecheck</code>, then <code>tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit</code> at the root.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>bun run desktop:dev</code></td>
          <td><code>build:sidecar</code>, then <code>tauri dev</code> in <code>@cadcamfun/desktop</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <code>@cadcamfun/mobile</code>’s own test script is <code>bun test test</code>, which only
      makes sense with the working directory <code>apps/mobile</code>. From the root, use
      <code>bun test apps/mobile</code> or <code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/mobile test</code>.
      iOS run scripts (<code>ios</code>, <code>ios:release</code>, <code>native:generate</code>)
      need Xcode. They are not part of <code>bun test packages apps</code>. WP13’s overview status
      says the Expo migration, gateway, pairing, and JS export are in place, and that native
      Release/device validation is in progress with TestFlight still pending. Do not describe
      TestFlight as shipped.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="avoid" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What not to import</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Import</th><th>Why it is rejected</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/db</code> from <code>packages/core</code> or <code>packages/api</code></td>
          <td>README rule. Those packages stay free of SQLite so they can run in tests and in the UI without a file.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@cadcamfun/db</code> from <code>apps/desktop</code> or <code>apps/mobile</code></td>
          <td>The window and the phone are HTTP clients. The sidecar owns the file.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Anything from <code>.reference/</code></td>
          <td>Git-ignored legacy tree. Domain knowledge only.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>effect</code> at a version other than <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code></td>
          <td>Service tags would split. nikcli’s SDK is built against this rc.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>A deep file under another package that is not in <code>exports</code></td>
          <td>The public surface is the package entry. Cross-package reach-ins break when the file moves.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>apps/sidecar</code> from <code>packages/core</code></td>
          <td>The arrow points the other way. Core has no I/O.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Degrees, or <code>Number.prototype.toString</code>, inside <code>packages/core</code></td>
          <td>Internal units are millimetres and radians. G-code uses a fixed decimal count (default 3).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The other direction is also a bug: a pass-through package that only re-exports the sidecar.
      Callers in the desktop import <code>@cadcamfun/api</code> types and talk HTTP. Callers in the
      sidecar import <code>@cadcamfun/db</code> and use <code>Database.query</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
